To work around #20096 we introduced a --hairpin-mode flag that flips cbr0 to promiscuous mode. Users of kubenet run with --configure-cbr0=false, so before we push kubenet to production we need to decide how to handle this. 

If we decided to stick with promiscuous mode, kubenet should set it on whatever bridge it creates. We will (hopefully) not have to continue relying on promiscuous mode on newer kernel versions. Maybe it still makes sense to do in the interim? or maybe we can push it down into the CNI bridge driver (unsure of a valid generic use case to make a bridge promiscuous)?

